{
  "rules": [
    "If sentiment is consistently positive (≥0.67) over recent days, model tends to overestimate prices; reduce forecast slope or add downward bias.",
    "If sentiment is consistently negative (≤0.33) or mixed, model often underestimates; increase forecast baseline or add upward bias.",
    "After a sharp price spike (e.g., >5% from prior peak), model frequently overshoots and fails to correct; apply a ‘cool-down’ correction to prevent overreaction.",
    "When true outcome shows strong mean reversion (e.g., rapid drop from 65+ to 55+), model often fails to recognize it; adjust forecast to reflect recent volatility and reversion tendency.",
    "If forecast is flat or trending upward with low sentiment, true outcome often drops; introduce a ‘sentiment-adjusted decay’ to reduce upward momentum when sentiment is weak.",
    "For 30-day horizon, model often fails to capture early sharp declines; add a ‘lagged sentiment filter’ to anticipate sudden drops based on prior sentiment shifts."
  ]
}
